{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen","id":1240946,"title":"The Realm Civil War: how does it happen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-31T10:46:43-07:00","id":1240946,"title":"The Realm Civil War: how does it happen?","content":"I keep trying to make this post, and then getting distracted and forgetting.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the best part of What Fire Has Wrought is the new vision of the Great Houses. I recall seeing a developer say that one of their goals was making the Houses as iconic as V:tM's clans, and I think they really succeeded! Reading the book I was struck by how dynamic and vital the whole thing feels. The relationships between the Houses are unbalanced; there's no sense of stasis. The whole thing is about to collapse, and there are distinct fracture-lines. <br /> <br /> To me, the fact that the Realm Civil War is THE looming threat again (rather than the Ebon Dragon's umpteenth escape plan) has made 3E my favorite edition. So! I wanted to start a thread where people throw out their ideas and timelines on how this looming threat plays out. Who strikes the first blow? Who betrays whom? What are the great upsets, the iconic battles, the devastating political plays, the desperate diplomatic missions? And who, at last, takes the Scarlet Throne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:23:22-07:00","id":1240968,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.<br /> Random ideas for how a civil war could start<br /> Two houses engage in brinkmanship over a disputed territory, a ship, etc. They misjudge each other, and accidentally start a war. Think Cuban Missile Crisis except nobody backs down. <br /> Something really stupid. A Dynast kills a Dynast from another house over a petty dispute, the victim's house demands recompense, it escalates. Think WWI.<br /> One of the more militarily powerful and economically weak house goes deep into debt/sells assets building an army in expectation of a war, realizes that they need to win the war before their economy collapses too far to maintain their army, and so starts trying to conquer satrapies and such from other Houses. Cathak and Peleps seem like the best cases, Sesus could but it's ties to Cynis protect it from this, Tepet is too militarily weak, maybe Ledaal or Mnemom. Ragara, Cynis, Nellens and V'neef seem to be in the opposite position.<br /> One house is near a have political or economic victory, they push forward with that, the other houses realize this is their last chance to not become subordinates. Mnemon is the most likely candidate here, but I could see Ragara or Peleps. <br /> Someone uncovers what they think is an immense advantage (the imperial manse, Ragara getting something out of their research, alliance with an outside power), and starts the war over that.<br /> A second house collapses (Nellens or V'neef, Ledaal tries and fails to reconquer Thorn/the Caul, Any house gets hit by an anathema-backed rebellion or Deathlord attack, Ragara is caught doing things they shouldn't), the other houses try to divvy it up like Tepet, but can't agree and start fighting over its remains.<br /> Someone executes a false flag - stage an attack on one house looking like it's from another, they start fighting. Iselsi might be in the best place to do this, but anyone who thinks they can't win a war but could take over from the exhausted combatants might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:06:19-07:00","id":1241003,"title":"","content":"Yeah, exactly! The obvious flashpoints for the Civil War that I see are: <br /> <br /> Ledaal/Ragara: Either Ledaal presents damning evidence of Ragara's corruption, or Ragara attacks Ledaal on a contrived pretext in order to head off just such a revelation. <br /> <br /> Peleps/V'Neef: This is, I think, the closest we have to a &quot;canon&quot; flashpoint. It's just a matter of time before all that Western brinksmanship goes too far and someone gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Sesus/Nellens: A Sesus spy ring is exposed attempting to undermine Nellens business and diplomacy fails. I could see the other Houses using this as an excuse to crush Nellens, and then conjuring further justifications for war from the conflict itself.<br /> <br /> Some other ones that come to mind are Cynis/Sesus (the intertwined blackmail network fails), and then like, Mnemon/everybody.<br /> <br /> When I have the time I'd really like to write-up a timeline of one of those scenarios. It's such a rich source of inspiration!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:16:19-07:00","id":1241062,"title":"","content":"I don't believe the Civil War will have a single, discrete flash-point. There are too many moving pieces, so I believe it more likely an intentional gambit to advance a House's position, falling afoul of some other House's machinations the first House is unaware of, triggering some larger multi-House response that escalates is likeliest. I realize D&amp;D is infamous in &quot;serious&quot; roleplaying circles, but the Forgotten Realms Drow House wars aren't a terrible parallel for what's going on with the Dynasty right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:45:32-07:00","id":1241107,"title":"","content":"Whether due to satrapial unrest, some unforeseen disaster, the PCs, or whatever else, one of the stronger/more connected Houses loses enough cash flow that it can\u2019t roll over its debt any more.<br /> <br /> Ragara tries to call the debt in and take a bunch of that House\u2019s stuff like they did with Tepet.<br /> <br /> This time though the debtor House says no.<br /> <br /> The first shot of the war is fired at a repo man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:31:37-07:00","id":1241141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241107#post1241107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether due to satrapial unrest, some unforeseen disaster, the PCs, or whatever else, one of the stronger/more connected Houses loses enough cash flow that it can\u2019t roll over its debt any more.<br /> <br /> Ragara tries to call the debt in and take a bunch of that House\u2019s stuff like they did with Tepet.<br /> <br /> This time though the debtor House says no.<br /> <br /> The first shot of the war is fired at a repo man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this theme: in an effort to repay/refinance some debt, one of the big houses makes a big, risky geopolitical play that sets off a conflagration. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T22:21:55-07:00","id":1241176,"title":"","content":"One thing I would really love to see change in EX3 would be (eventual) movement beyond RY 768. The imminent Civil War is a beloved, treasured plot device, but I wouldn't mind seeing canon movement forward. Even if it's packaged as a possibility-type supplement. Seeing what actual professional game designers would decide the Realm might look like post-Empress...I'd buy that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:36:09-07:00","id":1241232,"title":"","content":"There's gonna be something like that in Heirs of the Shogunate. It was a stretch goal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:43:52-07:00","id":1241234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241176#post1241176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I would really love to see change in EX3 would be (eventual) movement beyond RY 768. The imminent Civil War is a beloved, treasured plot device, but I wouldn't mind seeing canon movement forward. Even if it's packaged as a possibility-type supplement. Seeing what actual professional game designers would decide the Realm might look like post-Empress...I'd buy that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this could be very useful<br /> <br /> <br /> one way I often present the civil war to my players is either via rumors of - or direct encounters with - one of the two following: (only used in 2.5 games mind you)<br /> <br /> open warfare in the west, with various realm houses fighting for control of islands with critical iron mines. Naval battles with all the explosions and sorcery the local realm fleets can muster. Once the Denzik city ship reached the south, all of Creation learned of this.<br /> <br /> Another example - which can be applied anywhere really - is the example of a realm legion guarding a manse being constructed. The players would need some reason to go investigate, maybe to steal the cap-stones or something. There they would learn that the Ragara commander is basically keeping the Mnemon sorcerer-engineer overseeing the manse construction as prisoner - not letting her leave and exploiting her to build manses for house Ragara. Depending on what the players chose, this can result in a useful ally with a very open mind towards anathema, or it can simply be the players learning that something is wrong in the realm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:20:06-07:00","id":1241336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241141#post1241141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Building on this theme: in an effort to repay/refinance some debt, one of the big houses makes a big, risky geopolitical play that sets off a conflagration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm! Yes, I think &quot;Ragara calls in a debt&quot; is a solid pretext for war. If I'm remembering correctly, the book sets up Cathak as the potential foil for this scenario. But what would prompt Ragara to actually take the action? Again, the obvious precipitating event is Banoba getting cagey about Ledaal investigators, but maybe Sesus spy activity or Mnemon's success in Jiara might also force Ragara's hand. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm going to go back through WFHW and think about more detailed possibilities while I'm at work today ^__^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:46:31-07:00","id":1241414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241176#post1241176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I would really love to see change in EX3 would be (eventual) movement beyond RY 768. The imminent Civil War is a beloved, treasured plot device, but I wouldn't mind seeing canon movement forward. Even if it's packaged as a possibility-type supplement. Seeing what actual professional game designers would decide the Realm might look like post-Empress...I'd buy that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaplot does not work well in games where player characters are expected to have a major impact on the world; it's reliant on the timeline moving forward in one specific way that cannot be effectively interfered with, with later books building upon the foundation set by earlier books.<br /> <br /> Exalted is built on the idea that the player characters are superhuman demigods that will have a major impact on the world, often by murdering prominent NPCs and shattering what they've built, turning things that writers may want to make important for a storyline into complete non-factors at their table.<br /> <br /> I could definitely see a single supplement exploring all sorts of possibilities for the Realm Civil War simply due to how complex it could turn out to be even before non-Realm forces start to get involved (which they will), but a persistent metaplot would accomplish nothing but gradually making larger and larger sections of fluff completely useless for most groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T12:20:45-07:00","id":1241442,"title":"","content":"Since reading through WFHW I kind of got the impression that for a lot of the Great Houses step one in an open war between the houses will result in Ragara dying first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:45:00-07:00","id":1241477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241442#post1241442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since reading through WFHW I kind of got the impression that for a lot of the Great Houses step one in an open war between the houses will result in Ragara dying first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, but Ragara is both very rich already, and still a major creditor for all the other Houses. Ragara can certainly rope at least one other House into their defense by offering favorable terms on future loans, forgiveness of extant debts, bribes, or all three (not to mention whatever First Age lore they might choose to deploy). <br /> <br /> Yes, Ragara is a priority target, but they're far from an easy one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:11:04-07:00","id":1241488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241477#post1241477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, but Ragara is both very rich already, and still a major creditor for all the other Houses. Ragara can certainly rope at least one other House into their defense by offering favorable terms on future loans, forgiveness of extant debts, bribes, or all three (not to mention whatever First Age lore they might choose to deploy).<br /> <br /> Yes, Ragara is a priority target, but they're far from an easy one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh very much so, but I think Ragara is one of the Houses trying to avoid an open war partially to strengthen their own standing and also because of how hard it might be to convince another House to defend them when their destruction would both prevent a Ragara ruler and nullify said debt by virtue of no one remaining to claim said debts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:13:05-07:00","id":1241490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1240946-the-realm-civil-war-how-does-it-happen?p=1241477#post1241477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, but Ragara is both very rich already, and still a major creditor for all the other Houses. Ragara can certainly rope at least one other House into their defense by offering favorable terms on future loans, forgiveness of extant debts, bribes, or all three (not to mention whatever First Age lore they might choose to deploy).<br /> <br /> Yes, Ragara is a priority target, but they're far from an easy one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the people with all the money get ransacked first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:48:57-07:00","id":1241621,"title":"","content":"That's what I suggested, a possibility-type supplement. Although I'm not really sure that what Exalted is theme-wise anymore. The emphasis seems to be on reducing the power of the Exalted. &quot;Less Hercules, more Samson&quot; I read one developer write. That saddens me, personally. The decrease in the power-divide between Solars and individual DBs is something else I'm not thrilled by. I obviously haven't seen how Lunars/Sidereals/Alchemicals will fare yet, but I strongly suspect I'm going to be much unhappier as third progresses to include them.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with you though, concerning how &quot;canon meta-plot on rails&quot; is unworkable. The infamous 2E RotSE, with its unfortunate &quot;This is THE direction of events post-RY 768&quot; that gets created by the synergy of Under the Roseblack and RotSE, demonstrated that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}